          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Heroic Death</strong><br>\nLeonidas and his men fought to the death after being betrayed by a local resident who showed the Persians a way to outflank the Greek position. According to legend, Leonidas knew that death was certain and sent away the bulk of his army to preserve their strength for future battles, keeping only his 300 Spartans and a few hundred other troops.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Leonidas</strong><br>\nLeonidas's death became a symbol of courage and sacrifice. His decision to stand and die at Thermopylae became a rallying point for Greek resistance against Persian domination. It inspired the Greek city-states to unite against a common enemy, ultimately leading to Persian defeat in the Greco-Persian Wars.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cultural Impact</strong><br>\nLeonidas's story has had a lasting impact on Western culture, symbolizing the ideals of bravery and the willingness to fight against impossible odds. He has been depicted in various forms of art, literature, and popular media, including movies and video games, which celebrate his life and the values he stood for.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
